{
 "doc": "The skeleton's opcode table (RI-21 (4)): one row per opcode, its opcode the row's position + 1 (0 is reserved; the copy-only op, CCV_OP_PRF_COPY, is the all-ones code, outside the table). Rows are APPEND-ONLY: an opcode never moves, so a new row goes at the end, and its key (name, with _SEL<n> for an srd selector) is appended to `pinned` in the same change; tools/gen-ops.py refuses a row inserted, removed or reordered against `pinned`, a duplicated key and an unknown field. Each row names every field of struct OpInfo (sim/skel/stub.h) that has no default, and only the defaulted ones that differ from their default; `note` is the row's comment. tools/gen-ops.py writes sim/generated/ccv_ops.h (kOps) and rtl/generated/ccv_ops_pkg.sv (OP_<KEY> and ccv_op_attr(opcode)).",
